[
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"110050\">@Sébastien Gouëzel</span> we’re trying to navigate the relevant type class assumptions when doing Riemannian bundles and Riemannian manifolds, but Lean’s unification is not happy. Consider:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Mathlib</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Geometry</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Manifold</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">VectorBundle</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">CovariantDerivative</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Metric</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">open</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Bundle</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">section</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">variable</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">E</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">NormedAddCommGroup</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">E</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">NormedSpace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℝ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">E</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">H</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">TopologicalSpace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">H</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">I</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ModelWithCorners</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℝ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">E</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">H</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">M</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">TopologicalSpace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">M</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">ChartedSpace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">H</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">M</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">F</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">NormedAddCommGroup</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">F</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">NormedSpace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℝ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">F</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">FiniteDimensional</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℝ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">F</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">V</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">M</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">TopologicalSpace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">TotalSpace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">F</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">V</span><span class=\"o\">)]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"bp\">∀</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">AddCommGroup</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">V</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">)]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"bp\">∀</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Module</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℝ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">V</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">)]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"bp\">∀</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">M</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">TopologicalSpace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">V</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">)]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"bp\">∀</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">IsTopologicalAddGroup</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">V</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">)]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"bp\">∀</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ContinuousSMul</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℝ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">V</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">)]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">FiberBundle</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">F</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">V</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">VectorBundle</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℝ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">F</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">V</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">RiemannianBundle</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">V</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">IsContMDiffRiemannianBundle</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">I</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">F</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">V</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">ContMDiffVectorBundle</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">F</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">V</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">I</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">cov</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">CovariantDerivative</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">I</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">F</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">V</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n\n<span class=\"sd\">/-- info: cov.IsMetricCompatible : Prop -/</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">guard_msgs</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">in</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">check</span><span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">cov</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">IsMetricCompatible</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">end</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">section</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">variable</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">E</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">NormedAddCommGroup</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">E</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">NormedSpace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℝ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">E</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">FiniteDimensional</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℝ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">E</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">H</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">TopologicalSpace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">H</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">I</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ModelWithCorners</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℝ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">E</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">H</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">M</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">EMetricSpace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">M</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">ChartedSpace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">H</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">M</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">IsManifold</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">I</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">M</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">RiemannianBundle</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">M</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">↦</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">TangentSpace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">I</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">)]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">IsContMDiffRiemannianBundle</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">I</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">E</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">M</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">↦</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">TangentSpace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">I</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">)]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">cov</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">CovariantDerivative</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">I</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">E</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">TangentSpace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">I</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">M</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"o\">))</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">set_option</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">pp</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">mvars</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">anonymous</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">false</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">in</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">/--</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">error: Application type mismatch: The argument</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">  cov</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">has type</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">  @CovariantDerivative ℝ DenselyNormedField.toNontriviallyNormedField E inst✝⁸ inst✝⁷ H inst✝⁵ I M</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">    PseudoEMetricSpace.toUniformSpace.toTopologicalSpace inst✝³ E inst✝⁸ inst✝⁷ (TangentSpace I)</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">    instTopologicalSpaceTangentBundle (instAddCommGroupTangentSpace I) (instModuleTangentSpace I)</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">    (instTopologicalSpaceTangentSpace I) ⋯ ⋯ TangentSpace.fiberBundle</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">but is expected to have type</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">  @CovariantDerivative ℝ DenselyNormedField.toNontriviallyNormedField ?_ ?_ ?_ ?_ ?_ ?_ ?_ ?_ ?_ ?_ ?_ ?_ ?_ ?_</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">    (fun x =&gt; NormedAddCommGroup.toAddCommGroup) (fun x =&gt; InnerProductSpace.toNormedSpace.toModule)</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">    (fun x =&gt; PseudoMetricSpace.toUniformSpace.toTopologicalSpace) ⋯ ⋯ ?_</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">in the application</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">  @CovariantDerivative.IsMetricCompatible ?_ ?_ ?_ ?_ ?_ ?_ ?_ ?_ ?_ ?_ ?_ ?_ ?_ ?_ ?_ ?_ ?_ cov</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">-/</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">guard_msgs</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">in</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">check</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">cov</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">IsMetricCompatible</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"c1\">--(M := M) (V := TangentSpace I)</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">end</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>The first section works and is meant to be the recommended spelling for Riemannian vector bundles. The second section is meant to use the recommended spelling for Riemannian manifolds but the check is failing unless we give it the commented out implicit arguments. It’s weird that Lean cannot infer <code>M</code> and <code>V</code> despite having <code>cov</code>.  Any idea?</p>",
        "id": 605999672,
        "sender_full_name": "Patrick Massot",
        "timestamp": 1782220463
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Note every people who like weird unification issues are welcome to investigate, even without knowing differential geometry.</p>",
        "id": 605999974,
        "sender_full_name": "Patrick Massot",
        "timestamp": 1782220543
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Note that applying the following diff in <code>Mathlib/Geometry/Manifold/VectorBundle/CovariantDerivative/Metric.lean</code> fixes the example:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Diff\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"gi\">+  [∀ x, NormedAddCommGroup (V x)] [∀ x, InnerProductSpace ℝ (V x)] [FiberBundle F V]</span>\n<span class=\"gi\">+  [∀ x, AddCommGroup (V x)] [∀ x, Module ℝ (V x)]</span>\n<span class=\"gi\">+  [∀ x : M, TopologicalSpace (V x)]</span>\n<span class=\"gi\">+  [∀ x, IsTopologicalAddGroup (V x)] [∀ x, ContinuousSMul ℝ (V x)]</span>\n<span class=\"gi\">+  [FiberBundle F V] [RiemannianBundle V]</span>\n<span class=\"gd\">-  [∀ x, NormedAddCommGroup (V x)] [∀ x, InnerProductSpace ℝ (V x)] [FiberBundle F V]</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>as can be seen in <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/compare/master...grunweg:minimize-lcfailure\">https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/compare/master...grunweg:minimize-lcfailure</a>.</p>",
        "id": 606003271,
        "sender_full_name": "Michael Rothgang",
        "timestamp": 1782221199
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>... but that is actively undesirable, since it's not the right way to say \"Riemannian vector bundle\".<br>\n(edit to clarify: as Sebastien pointed out during review of the \"metric connections\" PRs.)</p>",
        "id": 606003442,
        "sender_full_name": "Michael Rothgang",
        "timestamp": 1782221237
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Running</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">set_option</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">trace</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">profiler</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">useHeartbeats</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">true</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">in</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">set_option</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">trace</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">profiler</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">true</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">in</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">check</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">cov</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">IsMetricCompatible</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>and unfolding, here are some telling things. We start with</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Elab</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">command</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"mf\">3416130.000000</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">💥️</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">check</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">cov</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">IsMetricCompatible</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">▶</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>i.e. \"it doesn't work\" and after unfolding we find</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Meta</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">isDefEq</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"mf\">167532.000000</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">❌️</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">CovariantDerivative</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">I</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">E</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">TangentSpace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">I</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=?=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">CovariantDerivative</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">?</span><span class=\"n\">m</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"m\">98</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">?</span><span class=\"n\">m</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"m\">102</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">?</span><span class=\"n\">m</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"m\">105</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">▶</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>which is bad, because it looks like there's a pretty obvious solution to this. So why does it fail? Unfolding this we see many green ticks, which looks good, and then another red X:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">[]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"mf\">86458.000000</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">❌️</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">instModuleTangentSpace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">I</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=?=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">↦</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">InnerProductSpace</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">toNormedSpace</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">toModule</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">▶</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>which looks bad because surely this should work. But actually let's go back and look at the last of the green ticks:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">[]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"mf\">32551.000000</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">✅️</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">instAddCommGroupTangentSpace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">I</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=?=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">↦</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">inst</span><span class=\"bp\">✝⁸.</span><span class=\"n\">toAddCommGroup</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">▶</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>This has worked but I don't think it's what you want. Because <code>inst✝⁸ : NormedAddCommGroup E</code> so I think this says \"typeclass inference has found a term of type <code>PseudoEMetricSpace.toUniformSpace.toTopologicalSpace inst✝³ : (_x : M) → AddCommGroup (TangentSpace I _x)</code> and it's \"the tangent space is defeq to E so let's use that\". Indeed, unfolding finds this at the bottom:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"w\">              </span><span class=\"o\">[]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"mf\">262.000000</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">✅️</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">AddCommGroup</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">E</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=?=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">AddCommGroup</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">TangentSpace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">I</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">▶</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>OK so now onto the failure:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">[]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"mf\">86458.000000</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">❌️</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">instModuleTangentSpace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">I</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=?=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">↦</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">InnerProductSpace</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">toNormedSpace</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">toModule</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">▶</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>Digging in, the cause of the failure is this failure of typeclass inference:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">synthInstance</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"mf\">165.000000</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">❌️</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">M</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">InnerProductSpace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℝ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">TangentSpace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">I</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">▶</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>and this failure is because we now have E's AddCommGroup structure on the tangent space so the attempt to use the inner product space you want fails.</p>",
        "id": 606028645,
        "sender_full_name": "Kevin Buzzard",
        "timestamp": 1782227142
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"110038\">Kevin Buzzard</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/287929-mathlib4/topic/Riemannian.20bundles.20issues.20again/near/606028645\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>which looks bad because surely this should work. But actually let's go back and look at the last of the green ticks:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">[]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"mf\">32551.000000</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">✅️</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">instAddCommGroupTangentSpace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">I</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=?=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">↦</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">inst</span><span class=\"bp\">✝⁸.</span><span class=\"n\">toAddCommGroup</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">▶</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>This has worked but I don't think it's what you want. Because <code>inst✝⁸ : NormedAddCommGroup E</code> so I think this says \"typeclass inference has found a term of type <code>PseudoEMetricSpace.toUniformSpace.toTopologicalSpace inst✝³ : (_x : M) → AddCommGroup (TangentSpace I _x)</code> and it's \"the tangent space is defeq to E so let's use that\".</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>It looks like the bug you had already hit the previous time, and that core has plans to fix but which haven't landed yet, right?</p>",
